Over on the blog. this week we had a post about bedwetting and scouts.

54
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
It's kind of a sensitive subject, I understand,

55
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:56,000
But nocturnal aneurysis or NE, is what we commonly call bedwetting.

56
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,000
It's involuntary urination during sleep

57
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:05,000
And this is something that is a very common condition amongst boys who are scouting age.

58
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,000
And I heard from a lot of you on that post.

59
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:14,000
I heard from Matt Price, who's with Scout Troop 444 in Fuqua Verena, North Carolina.

60
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:19,000
He said discussing this issue with parents. letting them know you're there to help is a great start

61
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
And I agree with you, Matt,

62
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,000
It's something that should be discussed.

63
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Mark Fisher checked in to say this is a great article.

64
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:31,000
As a longtime scoutmaster, I've had this issue come up a number of times.

65
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Pete Parris said we had a scout with NE at camp. before going to bed

66
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:42,000
I'd remind him to use latrine and then about 2 am we'd wake him up and make sure that he used latrine again,

67
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:46,000
And I always made sure another adult was awake too when we did this

68
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:50,000
And we didn't have an issue with any accidents using this method.

69
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Zane Neller got in touch to say it was a great article, Clark.

70
00:04:54,000 --> 00:05:00,000
I worked at a Weeblows camp for five years and we frequently had scouts in their first overnight camp setting who had this problem.

71
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:09,000
You do a great job of reminding us to empathize and make extra efforts to accommodate the scout so he can have a great week of camp.

72
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Also, remember that the camp staff sees this kind of thing and they'll always be willing to help you with access to laundry facilities or any other needs.

73
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:28,000
I would say that anybody who's worked on camp staff- and I did for a number of years knows that this can be a problem and you always want to help out.

74
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:36,000
That's another great resource for scouts who are dealing with any in one of their scouts to know that the camp staff is always willing to help you out.

75
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Bob Deck wrote to say over the 17 years I was a scout master. we had several scouts with any and I learned early on to take an extra sleeping bag or two when we went camping.

76
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:54,000
And that's also another great idea because there are going to be accidents and if you have a spare sleeping bag that can be a big help.

77
00:05:54,000 --> 00:06:04,000
I heard from Amber who said we had two scouts in our family who had NE and we worked diligently at home and in a year or so the problem fixed itself.

78
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:11,000
We have a scout in the troop now, but his parents don't really want to help with the plan, thinking that this is all going to go away.

79
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Any suggestions on what to do?

80
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:21,000
I think a good approach to have for this, Amber, would be telling parents that you know camping out is different than sleeping at home

81
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:27,000
And scouts- all scouts, whether they have NE or not- need the right gear to sleep comfortably.

82
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:30,000
They need a sleeping bag with the proper rating,

83
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
They need a sleeping pad.

84
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:39,000
Every scout needs that. but a scout with NE needs some other gear, especially if he's having accidents while he's camping.

85
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:49,000
So it's important to have the good nights or something similar, and if they don't send him with the right gear when he goes camping, it's going to be stressful and difficult for them.

86
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:56,000
And this whole subject matter, folks, the whole thing with NE- it's kind of an embarrassing, kind of sensitive situation.

87
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:04,000
But if you have a scout who's suffering with this condition, understand that it's very common condition and there's a lot that you can do about it.

