128
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:45,000
Scoutmastership in seven minutes or less.

129
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:57,000
So this is almost a trick question, but not really.

130
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Who are the most important volunteers in scouting?

131
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:06,000
These volunteers have more power and influence than council presidents

132
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:14,000
or commissioners or scoutmasters or cubmasters and all of the other volunteers put together.

133
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:20,000
Without the participation of these volunteers and without their support,

134
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:25,000
scouting would quickly just come to a complete halt.

135
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:30,000
The volunteers I'm talking about bring endless energy and resources

136
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:34,000
and real transformational power to their role in scouting.

137
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:38,000
They're the only volunteers we simply cannot afford to lose.

138
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:42,000
They are the most important volunteers in scouting.

139
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:45,000
So have you figured out who this is? yet

140
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:51,000
The single most important volunteers in scouting are the scouts themselves.

141
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:57,000
Scouts make a voluntary decision to participate in their packs and troops and crews from week to week.

142
00:11:57,000 --> 00:12:00,000
If the program they're participating in falls flat,

143
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:04,000
if it doesn't meet their expectations, if they're not getting something out of it,

144
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:07,000
they're going to stop volunteering their participation.

145
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:13,000
All of the time and effort and money and resources that adults dedicate to scouting

146
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:20,000
have absolutely no value if the scouts don't volunteer to participate right along with us, right.

147
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:26,000
Of course, the work that we scoutmasters and our fellow adult volunteers put into scouting is important,

148
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:34,000
but in many ways it's just not all that significant in comparison with what scouts volunteer to do.

149
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:38,000
So let's remember who the most important volunteers in scouting are.

150
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:42,000
We only have our positions, our volunteer positions,

151
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:47,000
to serve the interests and goals of the scouts and thus encourage their participation.

152
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:56,000
We must never lose sight of our role in serving the most important volunteers in scouting: the scouts themselves.

153
00:12:56,000 --> 00:13:01,000
Music,

154
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:04,000
Take me back to dream again.

155
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:07,000
By campfire on the trail,

